my $CODE = <<'END_CODE';
one
two
three
END_CODE

{
    desc => q{Ctrl-r redoes multiple undone operations},
    description => <<'END_DESC',
## Macro: `xt/visual/macros/redo_multiple`

Tests that repeated **Ctrl-r** commands redo multiple undone changes
in the correct order. Two lines are deleted, both are undone, then both
are redone.

**Keys:** `dd`, `dd`, `u`, `u`, `Control-r`, `Control-r`

**initial.png**
- Buffer has 3 lines: "one", "two", "three"
- Cursor on line 1

**after_both_dd.png**
- Buffer has 1 line: "three"
- First two lines deleted
- Intermediate snapshot after all deletions

**after_both_undo.png**
- Buffer restored to 3 lines (identical to initial)
- Both deletions undone
- Intermediate snapshot after all undos

**after_both_redo.png**
- Buffer back to 1 line: "three"
- Both deletions redone
- Same state as after_both_dd
END_DESC
    run => sub {
        my ($ctx) = @_;
        $ctx->buffer->set_text($CODE);
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('initial');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('dd');
        $ctx->delay(50);
        $ctx->keys('dd');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_both_dd');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('u');
        $ctx->delay(50);
        $ctx->keys('u');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_both_undo');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->keys('Control-r');
        $ctx->delay(50);
        $ctx->keys('Control-r');
        $ctx->delay(100);
        $ctx->snapshot('after_both_redo');
    },
}
